# scripts/macos/.gitignore
#
# restore.sh IS committed: it's generated, but it's the only record of the
# captured values, and committing it makes git the transport to a new Mac.

# Full domain exports are backup/reference only — bulky and redundant with
# restore.sh, so keep them local.
snapshot/*
# ...except the ones restore.sh actually reads back. capture.sh writes these
# as XML so they diff.
!snapshot/com.apple.symbolichotkeys.plist
!snapshot/NSGlobalDomain-NSUserKeyEquivalents.plist
